        "original_id": "3aacbeaa-4fc4-5ee1-982f-8af050906c52",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Home Rule League, Irish Parliamentary Party\n- Movements: Irish Home Rule movement\n- People: John Dunbar\n- Roles: Member of Parliament for New Ross\n- Places: Ireland, United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland\n\nFacts:\n- The Irish Home Rule movement agitated for self-government for Ireland within the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland.\n- The Home Rule League operated from 1873 to 1882 as a political party campaigning for home rule for Ireland within the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland.\n- The Home Rule League was also called the Home Rule Party or the Home Rule Confederation.\n- In February 1874, John Dunbar became the Home Rule League Member of Parliament for New Ross.\n- John Dunbar served as Member of Parliament for New Ross until his death in 1878.\n- The Irish Parliamentary Party replaced the Home Rule League.",
